# =============================================================================
# 1A1 Research Cell — environment configuration
# =============================================================================
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values from your Supabase
# project (Project Settings -> API). `.env.local` is gitignored and must never
# be committed.
#
# Nothing in this file is school-specific or developer-specific by design: to
# hand the project over, the school creates its own Supabase project and Vercel
# deployment and supplies its own values here. No credentials, emails or
# account identifiers are hard-coded anywhere in the source tree.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase — public values
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Safe to expose to the browser. The anon key carries no privileges of its own;
# every permission is enforced by Row Level Security in the database.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase — secret values
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEVER prefix this with NEXT_PUBLIC_. The service-role key bypasses all Row
# Level Security. It is read exclusively by modules marked `server-only`, so an
# accidental client import fails the build rather than leaking at runtime.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Site
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Canonical origin, used for redirects and absolute links. Set to the school's
# domain in production; no domain is assumed or hard-coded.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Environment label. Surfaced in the UI so a development instance is visually
# distinguishable from production and can never be mistaken for the live site.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ENV=development

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private CMS
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The management area is protected by ONE shared password, held by Research Cell
# leadership and school administration. There are no individual accounts.
#
# Generate this value with:
#
#     node scripts/hash-cms-password.mjs
#
# It is a scrypt hash, not the password. The password itself is never stored —
# keep it in the school's password manager. Rotating it means replacing this one
# value and redeploying; it does not touch the database.
CMS_PASSWORD_HASH=

# Once the shared password is accepted, the server signs in to Supabase as this
# account so that Row Level Security keeps enforcing every permission. It must
# be an existing account holding the school_admin role. Nobody is told these
# credentials and they never reach a browser — treat them like the service-role
# key. NEVER prefix either with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
CMS_SUPABASE_EMAIL=
CMS_SUPABASE_PASSWORD=
